266
00:21:38,501 --> 00:21:40,209
Well , my gauges must be wrong .

267
00:21:40,292 --> 00:21:42,001
I 've got a wind blowing due east .

268
00:21:42,084 --> 00:21:44,167
Now , what kind of a fog blows against the wind ?

269
00:21:44,626 --> 00:21:45,709
You got me .

270
00:21:45,792 --> 00:21:47,167
I 'm not so sure I want you .

271
00:21:47,292 --> 00:21:48,709
You 're just a voice on the phone .

272
00:21:49,209 --> 00:21:52,209
And you 're just a voice on the radio . We 'd make a perfect couple .

273
00:21:54,376 --> 00:21:56,751
You let me take you to dinner tonight , I 'll prove it to you .

274
00:21:57,792 --> 00:21:58,876
Sorry , Dan .

275
00:21:59,334 --> 00:22:01,751
My idea of perfection is a voice on the phone .

276
00:22:02,876 --> 00:22:03,959
OK , mystery lady .

277
00:22:05,417 --> 00:22:06,376
Good night .

278
00:22:06,542 --> 00:22:07,542
Good night .

279
00:22:28,459 --> 00:22:30,084
- Not bad . - [ chuckles ]

280
00:22:31,584 --> 00:22:33,459
I started a week ago in San Diego ,

281
00:22:34,126 --> 00:22:36,459
right up the coast , five drawings a day .

282
00:22:37,626 --> 00:22:39,209
It 'll probably take me a month to get to Vancouver ,

283
00:22:39,292 --> 00:22:41,667
and if I can sell ' em for five bucks apiece , I 'll be rich .

284
00:22:41,751 --> 00:22:44,209
[ laughs ] Yeah .

285
00:22:44,626 --> 00:22:45,501
Cool .

286
00:22:46,084 --> 00:22:47,959
- Can I ask you something ? - Sure .

287
00:22:48,084 --> 00:22:51,459
- What 's your name ? - Elizabeth .

288
00:22:51,542 --> 00:22:53,709
- Nick . - Hello , Nick .

289
00:22:54,584 --> 00:22:55,459
Hi .

290
00:22:57,542 --> 00:22:59,334
Is that where you 're from , San Diego ?

291
00:22:59,501 --> 00:23:01,792
Wait a minute . You said , " can I ask you something ? "

292
00:23:01,959 --> 00:23:05,501
Well , something to me means one thing . San Diego is two things .

293
00:23:05,584 --> 00:23:06,584
OK .

294
00:23:09,126 --> 00:23:11,959
Pasadena , and a lot of money .

295
00:23:13,626 --> 00:23:15,876
Never a chance to do anything I wanna do .

296
00:23:15,959 --> 00:23:17,042
Aww .

297
00:23:17,126 --> 00:23:18,751
[ mockingly ] Aww .

298
00:23:20,709 --> 00:23:22,167
What do you want to do ?

299
00:23:23,126 --> 00:23:24,042
I don 't know .

300
00:23:26,167 --> 00:23:27,667
That 's OK . Me neither .

301
00:23:29,334 --> 00:23:31,751
I think I got to have this one . Can I buy it ?

302
00:23:31,834 --> 00:23:35,126
Uh-uh . The drawing 's free .

303
00:23:38,626 --> 00:23:41,542
[ rhythmical knocking on door ]

304
00:23:43,667 --> 00:23:46,334
[ rhythmical knocking on door ]

305
00:23:55,001 --> 00:23:58,167
[ knocking continues ]

306
00:24:08,334 --> 00:24:11,084
- [ knocking ] - [ clock ticking ]

307
00:24:17,042 --> 00:24:20,084
[ clock chimes ]

308
00:24:20,959 --> 00:24:23,334
[ ominous music grows louder ]

309
00:24:26,876 --> 00:24:28,417
[ ominous music stops ]

310
00:24:31,126 --> 00:24:32,292
[ music playing on the radio ]

311
00:24:32,501 --> 00:24:34,417
[ Stevie ] It 's 1 : 00 , straight up ,

312
00:24:34,876 --> 00:24:36,084
the end of the witching hour

313
00:24:36,167 --> 00:24:38,167
and time for me to sign off .

314
00:24:40,126 --> 00:24:41,792
[ dog barking in distance ]

315
00:24:45,251 --> 00:24:47,167
So until tomorrow night , at 6 : 00 p.m. ,

316
00:24:47,251 --> 00:24:49,376
when KAB comes back on the air ,

317
00:24:49,917 --> 00:24:52,042
this is Stevie Wayne , your night light ,

318
00:24:52,417 --> 00:24:55,042
hoping you have a nice rest of the night .

319
00:24:56,001 --> 00:24:57,126
[ music fades out ]

320
00:25:00,251 --> 00:25:03,167
- [ seagulls screeching ] - [ wind blowing ]

321
00:26:15,584 --> 00:26:17,834
[ ominous music playing ]

322
00:26:17,917 --> 00:26:19,667
[ frogs croaking ]

323
00:26:49,792 --> 00:26:51,126
- [ music fades out ] - [ clock tolls ]

324
00:26:53,501 --> 00:26:56,501
[ shouts ] Mom ! Hey , mom !

325
00:26:59,001 --> 00:27:00,126
Mom !

326
00:27:00,501 --> 00:27:02,751
Mom , come on . Get up . Look what I found .

327
00:27:03,834 --> 00:27:07,167
Andy ... I love you ,

328
00:27:08,542 --> 00:27:10,209
but sometimes you 're a real pain .

329
00:27:10,626 --> 00:27:13,501
Sure , mom , but look it . First , it was a gold coin ,

330
00:27:13,584 --> 00:27:16,167
and then it turned into this neat piece of wood .

331
00:27:16,667 --> 00:27:19,751
- This is one of those times . - Uh-huh , but look at it , mom .

332
00:27:24,209 --> 00:27:27,459
Good morning , Andrew . Did you have a nice time last night ?

333
00:27:27,542 --> 00:27:30,459
Yeah . Old Mr. Machen told us ghost stories .

334
00:27:31,751 --> 00:27:33,917
Did you thank Mrs. Kobritz for bringing you home ?

335
00:27:34,001 --> 00:27:37,167
Yes , ma 'am . Mom , can I have a stomach pounder and a coke ?

336
00:27:38,542 --> 00:27:40,626
- After lunch . - OK .

337
00:27:40,792 --> 00:27:42,334
I 'm gonna go look for another one .

338
00:27:42,417 --> 00:27:44,334
Maybe this time I can get the gold coin .

339
00:27:58,292 --> 00:28:00,209
[ seagulls screeching ]

340
00:28:10,292 --> 00:28:11,167
Where the hell is he ?

341
00:28:11,542 --> 00:28:13,542
Rolled out of here at 4 : 15 yesterday .

342
00:28:13,626 --> 00:28:15,751
- That 's the last I saw of him . - Al said 7 : 30 , right here .

343
00:28:15,834 --> 00:28:17,792
Well , you know Al . If I were you , I 'd give myself - -

344
00:28:17,876 --> 00:28:19,376
Did you call the coast guard , Hank ?

345
00:28:19,751 --> 00:28:21,292
Nick , they probably got drunk last night .

346
00:28:21,376 --> 00:28:23,334
- They 're still out there ... - No , he wouldn 't do that .

347
00:28:23,417 --> 00:28:24,542
He 'd do anything .

348
00:28:24,626 --> 00:28:27,084
Al and I got drunk so many times together , I can 't count ' em all ,

349
00:28:27,167 --> 00:28:29,667
but we never got so shitfaced we couldn 't make it back in .

350
00:28:30,417 --> 00:28:33,417
He 's too good a sailor to stay out there all night and not let somebody know .

351
00:28:33,501 --> 00:28:36,126
- You sound like his wife . - Just his friend .

352
00:28:36,709 --> 00:28:38,376
- You worry too much , Nick . - Yeah .

353
00:28:41,084 --> 00:28:44,626
- Where are we going ? - I 'm going to talk Ashcroft

354
00:28:44,709 --> 00:28:47,251
into taking out his boat and looking for The Sea Grass .

355
00:28:47,334 --> 00:28:50,292
- Who 's Ashcroft ? - Someone who owes me a favor .

356
00:28:50,834 --> 00:28:52,001
Can I come along ?

357
00:28:53,251 --> 00:28:55,376
I thought you had to move on to Vancouver ?

358
00:28:55,459 --> 00:28:58,167
- Eventually . - Yeah .

359
00:29:01,209 --> 00:29:03,542
[ fanfare ]

360
00:29:04,126 --> 00:29:05,792
The sheriff will drive his own car .

361
00:29:05,876 --> 00:29:06,751
The mayor and his wife

362
00:29:06,876 --> 00:29:10,626
are to be picked up at 6 : 45 and brought to the mayor 's box .

363
00:29:11,001 --> 00:29:15,084
Then we 'll have speeches by the mayor , the sheriff , and me .

364
00:29:15,751 --> 00:29:17,417
- Oh , do you have my notes ? - Yes , ma 'am .

365
00:29:17,501 --> 00:29:20,917
Then we will pass out the candles and begin the procession .

366
00:29:21,209 --> 00:29:23,501
Then I will go home and pass out .

367
00:29:24,709 --> 00:29:26,417
I 'm almost afraid to look .

368
00:29:26,876 --> 00:29:28,042
Well ...

369
00:29:28,126 --> 00:29:30,959
[ man on P.A. ] Testing , testing .

370
00:29:31,042 --> 00:29:34,042
- Not bad . Not bad at all . - A work of art .

371
00:29:34,417 --> 00:29:37,626
Sandy , just be civil to me for another five hours .

372
00:29:37,792 --> 00:29:39,042
That 's all I ask .

373
00:29:39,542 --> 00:29:41,834
[ Mrs. Williams ] Let 's see now . Oh , the candles .

374
00:29:41,917 --> 00:29:43,834
Did you order the candles ? What a thought , a candlelight

375
00:29:43,917 --> 00:29:46,459
- procession with no candles . - [ sing-songy ] All taken care of .

376
00:29:47,042 --> 00:29:48,251
And the promotional material ...

377
00:29:48,334 --> 00:29:51,292
- Did you get that over to Stevie ? - Signed , sealed , and delivered .

378
00:29:51,751 --> 00:29:54,209
Sandy , you can be a very annoying person at times ,

379
00:29:54,292 --> 00:29:57,292
- but you do keep me together . - Thank you , Mrs. Williams .

380
00:29:59,001 --> 00:30:00,792
[ classical music playing ]

381
00:30:25,417 --> 00:30:26,792
[ changing station ]

382
00:30:26,876 --> 00:30:30,667
[ man on the radio ] Spivey Point . As of 1 : 57 today ,

383
00:30:31,209 --> 00:30:34,334
The Sea Grass had not responded to radio communication .

384
00:30:35,084 --> 00:30:38,334
The coast guard has begun a sweep South from Watley ,

385
00:30:38,417 --> 00:30:42,417
around Arcom Reef , and should be in the area of Spivey Point

386
00:30:42,584 --> 00:30:44,126
in approximately one hour .

387
00:30:45,251 --> 00:30:47,376
Repeating this bulletin from the coast guard ,

388
00:30:48,167 --> 00:30:51,917
be on the look out for The Sea Grass , a 30-foot trawler ,

389
00:30:52,084 --> 00:30:55,959
last seen approximately 15 miles east of Spivey Point .

390
00:30:56,876 --> 00:31:01,042
If you sight this vessel , please notify the coast guard immediately .

391
00:31:12,751 --> 00:31:15,667
- Nick , can I ask you a question ? - Yeah .

392
00:31:16,417 --> 00:31:18,834
- Is it always like this ? - It 's always different .

393
00:31:21,126 --> 00:31:23,376
- You 're worried , aren 't you ? - Yeah .

394
00:31:24,376 --> 00:31:25,834
She can get real mean .

395
00:31:26,501 --> 00:31:27,501
There .

396
00:31:31,417 --> 00:31:32,251
[ Nick ] Oh , yeah .

397
00:31:35,042 --> 00:31:36,042
Oh , yeah .

398
00:31:39,167 --> 00:31:41,709
[ Mrs. Williams ] Well , if I can just get through the speeches without yawning .

399
00:31:41,792 --> 00:31:44,167
- I couldn 't sleep last night . - [ Sandy ] Too excited ?

400
00:31:44,251 --> 00:31:46,709
No . Al went out on his boat last night and didn 't come home .

401
00:31:46,792 --> 00:31:49,417
- He still isn 't back . - Mrs. Williams !

402
00:31:49,501 --> 00:31:50,792
I called the coast guard , and they said ,

403
00:31:50,876 --> 00:31:52,959
" Oh , he might have had engine trouble . "

404
00:31:53,042 --> 00:31:54,042
They said not to worry .

405
00:31:55,084 --> 00:31:56,959
He was complaining about his boat last week .

406
00:31:57,042 --> 00:31:58,167
Maybe you ought to go home .

407
00:31:58,459 --> 00:32:00,834
Oh , that 's the last place I want to go .

408
00:32:00,917 --> 00:32:02,917
My dog started to bark at 12 : 00 last night

409
00:32:03,042 --> 00:32:04,917
and didn 't stop until 6 : 00 this morning .

410
00:32:05,042 --> 00:32:06,126
What happened ?

411
00:32:06,251 --> 00:32:08,251
He was pointed toward the ocean and growling .

412
00:32:08,334 --> 00:32:09,584
What does that tell you ?

413
00:32:09,792 --> 00:32:12,459
My dog goes crazy and decides to bark at the water .

414
00:32:12,584 --> 00:32:15,542
I heard the church bells at midnight as I started to drift off to sleep ,

415
00:32:15,626 --> 00:32:18,584
and suddenly , my car alarm went off for absolutely no reason .

416
00:32:18,667 --> 00:32:19,709
- Really ? - Uh-huh .

417
00:32:19,876 --> 00:32:23,084
Woke up the whole block . This town sits around for 100 years

418
00:32:23,167 --> 00:32:26,167
and nothing happens , and then one night , the whole place falls apart .

419
00:32:26,751 --> 00:32:27,626
Al ?

420
00:32:28,917 --> 00:32:30,167
Take this line , too .

421
00:32:31,501 --> 00:32:34,834
[ shouts ] Al ! Tommy ! Dick !

422
00:32:39,917 --> 00:32:41,667
Cabin and steering house are empty .

423
00:32:42,459 --> 00:32:43,917
Maybe somebody picked them up .

424
00:32:46,292 --> 00:32:49,667
- There 's water in the generator . - But the deck is as dry as a bone .

425
00:32:49,751 --> 00:32:52,126
[ ominous music playing ]

426
00:33:16,542 --> 00:33:19,792
[ Mrs. Williams ] There you have it . My next project , restoration

427
00:33:19,876 --> 00:33:22,792
of the Morgantown Road Cemetery . It 's historical .

428
00:33:22,876 --> 00:33:24,751
- Our ancestors are buried here . - It 's gonna cost a lot .

429
00:33:24,834 --> 00:33:28,126
Come on , Sandy . So ? This town should be proud of its past .

430
00:33:28,209 --> 00:33:32,042
But trying to get anyone involved in community affairs is like pulling teeth .

431
00:33:32,709 --> 00:33:34,959
Better get the estimates ready for the council meeting next month .

432
00:33:35,042 --> 00:33:35,876
Yes , ma 'am .

433
00:33:36,292 --> 00:33:38,459
Sandy , you 're the only person I know who can make

434
00:33:38,542 --> 00:33:40,126
" yes , ma 'am " sound like " screw you . "

435
00:33:40,251 --> 00:33:41,251
Yes , ma 'am .

436
00:33:41,417 --> 00:33:44,084
Now , if we 'll just say a little prayer asking that he not be in his cups .

437
00:33:47,292 --> 00:33:48,626
[ doors creaking ]

438
00:33:51,459 --> 00:33:52,876
Not a good sign .

439
00:33:56,167 --> 00:33:59,459
[ sing-songy ] Father Malone ? Father Malone !

440
00:34:00,876 --> 00:34:02,167
[ doors creaking ]

441
00:34:04,751 --> 00:34:07,751
- Hello ! - Another bad sign .

442
00:34:08,417 --> 00:34:10,501
You try the study , and I 'll look up front .

443
00:34:31,917 --> 00:34:32,792
Father Malone !

444
00:34:35,167 --> 00:34:38,084
- Jesus ! - I 'm sorry , Mrs. Williams .

445
00:34:38,876 --> 00:34:40,209
- Mrs. Williams ... - Are you all right ?

446
00:34:41,959 --> 00:34:43,459
I have something to show you .

447
00:34:43,542 --> 00:34:45,542
[ ominous music playing ]

448
00:34:49,417 --> 00:34:50,542
" December 9 .

449
00:34:52,167 --> 00:34:54,792
Met with Blake this evening for the first time .

450
00:34:56,084 --> 00:34:57,292
He stood in the shadows

451
00:34:57,376 --> 00:35:00,042
to prevent me from getting a clear look at his face .

452
00:35:01,792 --> 00:35:03,709
What a vile disease this is .

453
00:35:05,126 --> 00:35:07,751
He is a rich man with a cursed condition ,

454
00:35:09,126 --> 00:35:12,626
but this does not prevent him from trying to better his situation

455
00:35:12,709 --> 00:35:14,917
and that of his comrades at the colony . "

456
00:35:35,917 --> 00:35:37,626
Every single gauge is broken .

457
00:35:40,667 --> 00:35:42,542
- All the glass is shattered . - Remind you of something ?

458
00:35:42,917 --> 00:35:44,209
- Last night . - Your truck .

459
00:35:44,292 --> 00:35:47,209
Yeah . Yeah .

460
00:35:53,584 --> 00:35:54,709
Thermometer 's broken .

461
00:35:57,251 --> 00:35:59,167
The mercury 's stuck at 20 degrees .

462
00:36:02,542 --> 00:36:03,792
There 's no water got in here ,

463
00:36:03,876 --> 00:36:05,626
but something awful cold did .

464
00:36:07,126 --> 00:36:10,417
" December 11 . Blake 's proposition is simple .

465
00:36:11,459 --> 00:36:13,626
He wants to move off Tanzier Island

466
00:36:13,709 --> 00:36:17,542
and relocate the entire colony just north of here .

467
00:36:18,626 --> 00:36:20,584
He has purchased a clipper ship

468
00:36:20,751 --> 00:36:23,917
called the Elizabeth Dane .

469
00:36:24,501 --> 00:36:26,001
With part of his fortune

470
00:36:26,084 --> 00:36:28,834
and asks only for permission to settle here .

471
00:36:29,959 --> 00:36:33,042
I must balance my feelings of mercy and compassion

472
00:36:33,126 --> 00:36:37,417
toward this poor man with my revulsion at the thought

473
00:36:37,501 --> 00:36:40,084
of a leper colony only a mile distant . "

474
00:36:59,126 --> 00:37:00,667
It 's rusted to the wall .

475
00:37:01,626 --> 00:37:03,042
[ radio static ]

476
00:37:04,876 --> 00:37:05,792
It was on .

477
00:37:14,459 --> 00:37:16,876
- They drank a lot of beer last night . - Every night .

478
00:37:18,126 --> 00:37:19,084
What 's it like ?

479
00:37:20,417 --> 00:37:22,584
It 's always the same . Room starts spinning - -

480
00:37:22,667 --> 00:37:23,751
I mean fishing .

481
00:37:25,542 --> 00:37:26,709
[ clears throat ]

482
00:37:27,626 --> 00:37:28,876
You fish .

483
00:37:28,959 --> 00:37:31,501
The only thing I know about fishing is you use a lot of worms .

484
00:37:31,584 --> 00:37:32,501
Hmm .

485
00:37:34,251 --> 00:37:35,126
Salt water .

486
00:37:37,959 --> 00:37:40,501
She was clean 2 nights ago . I checked her out myself .

487
00:37:40,584 --> 00:37:42,917
And now it 's as if she 's been turned over in the water .

488
00:37:46,501 --> 00:37:49,209
" April 20 . The six of us met tonight .

489
00:37:50,292 --> 00:37:51,876
From midnight until 1 : 00 ,

490
00:37:51,959 --> 00:37:55,376
we planned the death of Blake and his comrades .

491
00:37:56,542 --> 00:38:00,084
I tell myself that Blake 's gold will allow the church to be built

492
00:38:00,167 --> 00:38:02,876
and our small settlement to become a township ,

493
00:38:03,001 --> 00:38:06,042
but it does not soothe the horror that I feel

494
00:38:06,459 --> 00:38:09,209
being an accomplice to murder . "

495
00:38:12,751 --> 00:38:15,959
[ sighs ] Now what ?

496
00:38:16,834 --> 00:38:18,126
Wait for the coast guard .

497
00:38:23,334 --> 00:38:26,292
- I 'm sorry . - What for ?

498
00:38:26,876 --> 00:38:28,959
Ever since you picked me up , things have been going wrong .

499
00:38:29,376 --> 00:38:31,584
The clock broke , the windows have been breaking .

500
00:38:31,876 --> 00:38:34,501
- The weirdo at the door last night . - That isn 't you .

501
00:38:34,667 --> 00:38:35,542
I 'm not so sure .

502
00:38:36,876 --> 00:38:40,209
Things seem to happen to me . I 'm bad luck .

503
00:38:42,584 --> 00:38:45,626
I don 't believe in luck , good or bad .

504
00:38:47,167 --> 00:38:48,834
I don 't believe in anything much .

505
00:38:51,917 --> 00:38:53,709
Something did happen once .

506
00:38:56,917 --> 00:38:58,584
My father was a fisherman .

507
00:38:59,667 --> 00:39:02,459
He ran a trawler out of Whitely Reef .

508
00:39:03,917 --> 00:39:07,417
One night , late , he was coming back in .

509
00:39:08,084 --> 00:39:10,459
He was out beyond the reef , out near Spivey Point .

510
00:39:12,501 --> 00:39:13,709
He looked to windward

511
00:39:14,834 --> 00:39:16,876
and saw a brig under shortsail

512
00:39:18,626 --> 00:39:19,792
heading right for him .

513
00:39:23,334 --> 00:39:25,626
And he radioed . There was no reply .

514
00:39:27,209 --> 00:39:30,834
Nothing moved on the deck , but she held her course .

515
00:39:33,167 --> 00:39:34,292
My dad and two of his hands ,

516
00:39:34,459 --> 00:39:38,001
they boarded the brig ... The Resa Jane .

517
00:39:39,126 --> 00:39:40,792
No one was on board .

518
00:39:42,667 --> 00:39:46,126
There was food on the table ... and a hot , steaming cup of coffee .

519
00:39:46,292 --> 00:39:50,417
But underneath , a tin cup was rusted to the table .

520
00:39:51,667 --> 00:39:53,584
And then something caught my father 's eye .

